# Score files here are ignored by default, and the corpus is force-added.
#
# This directory is where someone drops a score to test the importer against,
# and the repertoire that is most useful for that is usually under copyright.
# This is a public repository, so the default has to be "not committed": the
# README's "add it with git add -f" step is what makes committing a corpus file
# a deliberate act, and this file is what makes it one.
#
# Already-tracked files are unaffected by this -- the thirty-six corpus scores
# stay exactly as they are -- so the rule only governs what arrives next.
*.mxl
*.musicxml
*.xml
